{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/mergeRemote(into:ids:deleted:policy:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Re-hydration restricted to the rows a caller already knows changed."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","text":"MainActor","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mergeRemote","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"into","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"store","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux5StoreC","text":"Store","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"State","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ids","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh","text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV","text":"UUID","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"deleted","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh","text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV","text":"UUID","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"> = [], "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"policy"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MergePolicy","preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiduxPersistence11MergePolicyV","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"}]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The live store to reconcile.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"store"},{"name":"ids","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The identities to re-read. IDs matching no row, and IDs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"belonging to another entity type, are harmless.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"deleted","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Identities known to have been deleted elsewhere.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"policy","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Narrows the configured policy for this call only.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The O(k) counterpart to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which re-reads every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row of every registered entity on every tick. Where a sync signal carries","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"which","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" identities changed, this spends that knowledge: one batched fetch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per 500 IDs instead of a full-table scan, and only the named entities are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reconciled. Everything else in state is left exactly as it was.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every guarantee "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)"},{"type":"text","text":" makes holds here. Pending"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"writes are flushed first; an ID with unflushed local intent — a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drained-but-unflushed write, an un-drained edit, a pending deletion, a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"write whose save failed, or an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/editing"},{"text":" hold — always wins, and that is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not configurable.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"important","name":"Important","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A partial read cannot tell a deleted row from one that was","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never asked about, so this ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"never"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" infers a deletion. An ID vanishes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only if you name it in ","type":"text"},{"code":"deleted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and only if the resolved policy grants"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy\/removesMissingEntities"},{"type":"text","text":". Name only what you have positive"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"evidence for — a history tombstone, not an empty fetch. In exchange,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"there is no empty-snapshot guard to work around: this can remove the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"last surviving entity, which ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An ID named in "},{"code":"deleted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that storage "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"still holds","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is not removed. A live"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row is evidence the deletion was itself undone elsewhere; a tombstone can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be stale."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Deferred-rows-are-re-offered","text":"Deferred rows are re-offered","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tick may read a row and decline to apply it — an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/editing"},{"type":"text","text":" hold is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one exemption that leaves no other trace. Those rows are remembered by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identity and re-offered on the next call, on top of whatever "},{"code":"ids","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" names,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so a caller does not have to re-queue them against its own signal. That"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"matters here because a sync signal is generally not resent and releasing a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hold writes no transaction of its own, so without it a hold would quietly","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"become a veto. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/mergeChanges(into:policy:)"},{"text":" shares the same debt, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"either path settles what the other deferred. Both discard it when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"container is swapped.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Registered ","type":"text"},{"code":"collapse:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" resolvers do not run here — a resolver is handed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the whole table and asked which rows survive, and a subset would have it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"judge a world it cannot see. Duplicate rows are still collapsed on read","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and still reported. Use ","type":"text"},{"code":"collapseDuplicates(into:)-(Store)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or a full","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)"},{"text":" to reclaim them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","title":"mergeRemote(into:ids:deleted:policy:)","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}]},"extendedModule":"SwiduxPersistence","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mergeRemote","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"into","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux5StoreC","text":"Store","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"State","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ids","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh","tex